package com.bmscompanion.app.data.wdp

/**
 * The 72 MFD page selectors of WDP's DTC page, as data: which display (mode 0 A-G … 5 S-J, MFD 0–3, 0 left /
 * 1 centre / 2 right) each writes, and the eleven "if that box shows what this one shows, blank it" tests its
 * SelectedIndexChanged handler runs, in its order. Read out of Falcas's handlers rather than written as a loop,
 * because they are not all alike: every centre selector of the first two MFDs compares the fourth MFD's boxes with
 * that MFD's LEFT selector instead of itself, and the third A-A MFD's centre selector tests the A-G page's left box.
 *
 * The page takes only the first four fields from here (which box writes which display). Its blanking is one rule
 * instead — any other box of the same master mode showing the page just chosen is blanked (D14, see [DtcPage]) —
 * and [Sel.clears] is kept as WDP's own behaviour, for the checks that show where the two part.
